<h2>3. Detailed Case-by-Case End-to-End Validation Logs</h2><p><i>The following dialogues reflect the exact automated representative transcripts generated on production and validated in the UI:</i></p><h3>Use Case 1: Buyer Looking for Product Supplier (RFQ Product)</h3>
    <p>
      <b>Inquiry Type:</b> <tt>RFQ_PRODUCT</tt> &nbsp;|&nbsp;
      <b>Status:</b> <span class="badge-pass">PASSED (All 5 Autonomous Turns Verified)</span><br>
      <b>Initiator:</b> <tt>sanjanamaahi</tt> (InfraTech EPC Solutions Ltd) &rarr; 
      <b>Target:</b> <tt>maahi</tt> (Maahi Decarb Materials Pvt Ltd)<br>
      <b>Live Conversation ID:</b> <tt>330cf9f9-d9d8-4d58-8c78-8bc26c9ab3ca</tt>
    </p>
    <p><b>Business Context:</b> An EPC contractor (InfraTech EPC Solutions Ltd) requires 1,000 MT of certified Limestone Calcined Clay Cement (LC3) for upcoming green infrastructure projects in Pune.</p>
    <p><b>What Is Being Tested:</b> Tests standard physical product procurement RFQ, declared plant run-rate capacity validation (2,500 MT/mo), Ex Works price quotation disclosure (&#8377;4,900 - &#8377;5,100/MT), Mill Test Certificate (MTC) assurance, and smooth 5th-turn executive handover.</p>

    <table>
      <thead>
        <tr><th colspan="2">Declared Commercial Parameters</th></tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td width="30%"><b>Product / Service Name</b></td><td>Limestone Calcined Clay Cement (LC3)</td></tr>
        <tr><td><b>Taxonomy / Grade Code</b></td><td><tt>CALCINED_CLAY_LC3 LC3_50_STANDARD</tt></td></tr>
        <tr><td><b>Quantity &amp; Unit</b></td><td>1,000.0 METRIC_TONNE</td></tr>
        <tr><td><b>Delivery Location &amp; Timeline</b></td><td>Pune &nbsp;|&nbsp; 30 Days (PLANNED)</td></tr>
        <tr><td><b>Inquiry Notes</b></td><td><i>&ldquo;Exploring supply availability and batch test certification for commercial infrastructure project.&rdquo;</i></td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>

    <p><b>Autonomous Representative Dialogue (5 Turns):</b></p>
    
        <div class="turn-card">
          <div class="turn-title">&#129302; Turn #1 &mdash; InfraTech EPC Solutions Ltd's Representative</div>
          <div class="turn-content">&ldquo;Hello Maahi Sharma, I am representing Mahajan Sanjana (InfraTech EPC Solutions Ltd). In line with our active preference of exploring sustainable cement blends and bulker logistics contracts for Western Maharashtra projects, we have submitted a formal procurement inquiry for 1,000 METRIC TONNE of Limestone Calcined Clay Cement (LC3) for delivery to Pune within 30 days. Project requirement notes: 'Exploring supply availability and batch test certification for commercial infrastructure project.'. Could your virtual representative confirm production run-rate capacity, dispatch lead times, and current indicative pricing?&rdquo;</div>
        </div>
        
        <div class="turn-card">
          <div class="turn-title">&#129302; Turn #2 &mdash; Maahi Decarb Materials Pvt Ltd's Representative</div>
          <div class="turn-content">&ldquo;Hello Mahajan Sanjana, representing Maahi Sharma at Maahi Decarb Materials Pvt Ltd. Aligned with our active focus on annual cement supply agreements and regional distributor alliances, we confirm commercial capability for Limestone Calcined Clay Cement (LC3). Our declared production capacity is 2,500 METRIC TONNE / month with delivery coverage across Pune, Mumbai, Nashik. Dispatch lead time is approximately 5 days from order confirmation. Uncommitted allocation is unrecorded and will be verified directly by our dispatch team. Our current indicative price range is &#8377;4,900 - &#8377;5,100 / METRIC TONNE (Ex Works).&rdquo;</div>
        </div>
        
        <div class="turn-card">
          <div class="turn-title">&#129302; Turn #3 &mdash; InfraTech EPC Solutions Ltd's Representative</div>
          <div class="turn-content">&ldquo;Thank you for confirming capacity and operational scope. To align with our project specifications, could you confirm test certificate availability (such as batch test reports or standard laboratory compliance) and packaging options (bulk pneumatic tanker vs standard packaging)? Also, please clarify whether quotation terms operate Ex-Works or delivered to site in Pune.&rdquo;</div>
        </div>
        
        <div class="turn-card">
          <div class="turn-title">&#129302; Turn #4 &mdash; Maahi Decarb Materials Pvt Ltd's Representative</div>
          <div class="turn-content">&ldquo;Regarding quality and terms: We provide standard manufacturer test certificates (MTC) and batch compliance reports with every dispatch. We support pneumatic bulker tanker dispatches as well as standard packaging. Commercial pricing basis is typically confirmed on an Ex-Works basis with carrier freight transit coordinated directly to Pune. Dispatch schedules can be scheduled in phases to meet your 30-day timeline.&rdquo;</div>
        </div>
        
        <div class="turn-card">
          <div class="turn-title">&#129302; Turn #5 &mdash; InfraTech EPC Solutions Ltd's Representative</div>
          <div class="turn-content">&ldquo;Commercial RFQ dialogue complete: 1,000 METRIC TONNE of Limestone Calcined Clay Cement (LC3) for delivery to Pune within 30 days. Supplier run-rate capacity (2,500 METRIC TONNE / month) and lead time (5 days) verified. I will now hand over this channel directly to Mahajan Sanjana and Maahi Sharma to finalize commercial contract terms, purchase orders, and delivery paperwork. Best regards!&rdquo;</div>
        </div>
        
    <div class="audit-box">
      &#10004; <b>Grounding Verification:</b> Verified against catalog declarations. Run-rate capacity, dispatch lead times, and indicative pricing quoted strictly within verified boundaries with zero fabricated claims.
    </div>
    <hr style="border: 0; border-top: 1pt solid #e5e7eb; margin: 18pt 0;">
